f  followers bonnie has burn scars all over  her shoulders and back from a childhood  accident and is undergoing extremely  painful experimental gene therapy to try  and remove them nancy lives in a rundown  trailer with her alcoholic mother grace  and her abusive stepfather ray the next  day the three invite sarah on a field  trip which she accepts and the group  takes a bus out to the desolate woods  deep in the woods sarah rochelle nancy  and bonnie begin a ceremony that  officially establishes their circle they  hold each other at knife point while  reciting an incantation the four witches  then pierce their index fingers and mix  their blood with wine performing their  first group spell they each drink in  turn asking meno for what their hearts  desire rochelle wants revenge on laura  sarah wants chris to return her  affections and bonnie wants to be  beautiful on the outside as well as him  nancy however dreams a little bit bigger  within a matter of hours sarah's love  spell on chris begins working and she  manipulates his new obsession to  humiliate him in retaliation the coven  decides to further test their abilities  by playing light as a feather stiff as a  board the result of which undoubtedly  confirms the presence of supernatural  intervention the next day when laura  bullies rochelle her signature blonde  quaff immediately starts falling out  then at her next doctor's appointment  bonnie's scars melt off her body with  impossible ease leaving the doctor  speechless the magic is working  for everyone but nancy that is  frustrated by manol's lack of  intervention until now nancy returns to  her dysfunctional family but a violent  encounter that ends in her stepfather  dying of a heart attack seems to prove  that her prayers have not been ignored  after all a life insurance policy leaves  nancy and her mother  175 000  which they used to move into fancier  digs downtown at nancy's new apartment  the witches practice glamouring a type  of spell that can change outward  appearances with just a bit of  concentration all is not well in the  witches world however sarah's love spell  seems to have been too effective turning  chris's newfound desire into a dangerous  obsession sarah consults lyrio for  advice on how to break the spell but she  learns an unfortunate truth about  witchcraft a spell must run its course  she also learns about the law of karmic  justice at the beach at twilight the  coven arrives with their familiars as  they prepare to invoke the spirit of men  here sarah opens up some more about her  past specifically that she used to  hallucinate snakes and insects around  the time of her suicide attempt unfazed  nancy leads an incredibly intense  ceremony that provokes lightning and  wind as the women chant the next morning  they awaken on the beach to find nancy  walking on water and a horde of dead  sharks washed ashore  sarah understandably freaked out by the  invocation ceremony tries to talk sense  into the other three witches but they're  all drunk on nancy's power even though  rochelle experiences some remorse when  she sees laura having a panic attack  over her balding scalp it's three  against one and nancy is starting to  think that maybe sarah shouldn't be part  of the coven after all feeling lost and  afraid sarah turns to chris for support  even though his obsession is reaching  dangerous levels she agrees to go out  with him for dinner but instead chris  takes her to a remote spot where he  sexually assaults her sarah manages to  escape to rochelle's house and tells the  other witches what happened and in a fit  of rage nancy lures chris upstairs at a  nearby party and glamours herself into  sarah when the real sarah breaks the  glamour and chris is dismissive once  again nancy loses it she throws chris  out a window with her mind killing him  instantly  in the wake of chris's death which  everyone conveniently thinks was an  accident sarah breaks with the coven  entirely she cuts nancy out of a group  photo and attempts to do a binding spell  that would prevent nancy from hurting  anyone else or herself unfortunately for  sarah the power of meno has given nancy  the ability to read her mind and torment  her with terrible dreams and  hallucinations at school nancy bonnie  and rochelle accost sarah in the  bathroom telling her that they were all  interviewed by police following chris's  death nancy argues that rey and chris  deserve to die and if sarah wants to  leave the coven she'd better watch her  back desperate sarah gosselin at the  occult shop for help and explains her  predicament lyrio invites sarah into the  secret back room a pagan temple built on  a place of power she lights all the  candles with one match and tells sarah  she's from a long line of witches and  needs to invoke manol herself before  illyrio can help any further however  nancy disrupts the ceremony astrally  forcing sarah to retreat home  sarah arrives at an empty house and  finds out that her father and stepmother  flew to san francisco thinking that  sarah had run away unbelievably their  plane crashed killing everyone on board  just when sarah thinks things couldn't  get any worse the house starts filling  with snakes bugs rats and all sorts of  creepy crawlies the creatures chase  sarah until she's face to face with  nancy who reveals that the whole thing  was a glamour and that she's planning on  staging sarah's suicide desperate to  fight back sarah is forced to invoke the  spirit of manol herself in the process  she gives bonnie and rochelle a taste of  their own medicine with the law of karma  and the two run away in fear sarah  finishes invoking the spirit and uses  the opportunity to torment nazi the same  way she tormented her using all sorts of  glamours and tricky spells nancy tries  to kill sarah but with her newly invoked  powers sarah is able to successfully  bind nancy and end their showdown for  good days later bonnie and rochelle  visit sarah to apologize for their  actions during the confrontation they  reveal they've lost their powers but  that doesn't stop sarah from using her  abilities to try and crush them with a  tree branch finally the craft ends with  nancy in a mental institution shouting  about the power of manol as she's being  restrained and sedated  while the craft is framed as a movie  about four young witches with new girl  sarah bailey at center over the years  the discourse surrounding the film has  deepened considerably to propose the  notion that sarah might in fact be the  bad guy here for one sarah abandons her  sisters on several occasions to run back  to chris hooker the guy who spread a  nasty rumor about her right at the start  even after chris tries to sexually  assault sarah and nancy kills him in  retaliation sarah still tries to defend  him  say what by the end of the craft when  sarah has invoked the spirit of menol  instead of trying to help the nancy with  her newfound powers she taunts her with  the same manipulations that nancy used  on her effectively driving her mad by  the film's end she also ends the film by  threatening bonnie and rochelle even  after they confessed to losing their  powers it seems as if sarah took her  powers to as dark a place as nancy's  went but for whatever reason she's  allowed to get away with it  if sarah is the actual villain of the  craft then we need to reassess her foil  nancy downs nancy starts the film living  in a trailer park where her stepdad  regularly abuses her alcoholic mother  their electricity is often out since  they can't pay their bills and there's  even a hole in the roof over nancy's bed  tripping water on her face as she tries  to sleep the implication is that nancy  is a scholarship student at the elite st  benedict's catholic school and that she  spends her free time casting spells to  try and lift her and her mother out of  poverty on top of all that nancy was  given an std and abandoned by chris  hooker not to mention how often rey  seems to violate her bodily autonomy the  link between poverty a lack of health  care and possible underlying mental  illness combined with dabbling in the  occult was a devastating cocktail for  nancy she wanted the power to change her  life and circumstances but she didn't  know how to do it without using  supernatural means even when she and her  mom came into a considerable amount of  money nancy still isn't able to address  her root traumas  that said the craft has a far more  ambiguous ending than people think  thanks to sarah's spell nancy is only  bound against hurting herself and others  not against using magic as a whole if  she'd been able to gather her thoughts  and regroup internally she could realize  that she still has access to menaul's  power this could change her  circumstances for the better once again  even without violence furthermore a  spell only lasts as long as the witch  who cast it lives so if sarah dies  before nancy nancy could be walking on  water again in no time  on the surface the craft is a story  about young women coming into personal  and collective power through magic  however this camaraderie only lasts  briefly and it's not long before the  four women involved all turn on each  other in vicious ways first nancy's  ongoing jealousy of sarah's natural  powers turns into a disaster as sarah  tries to guide the group's growing magic  down which she considers healthier paths  as the divide between nancy and sarah  grows bonnie and rachelle choose the  side of power and stick with nancy even  as she becomes increasingly erratic and  violent once sarah has had enough the  other three mercilessly bully her just  as they've been tormented by others  culminating in a truly grotesque plan to  kill sarah and stage it as a suicide  nancy exploits vulnerable information  about sarah's suicide attempt  information that was told her in  confidence to further torture her even  after sarah helps wake bonnie and  rochelle up to their bad behavior they  still only apologize because they've  lost their powers and want them back the  craft ends with sarah cutting off  rochelle and bonnie while poor nancy is  locked up in a mental institution if it  isn't already obvious the craft is more  about fraught and toxic relationships  between women than female friends who  actually empower each other if you or  anyone you know is having suicidal  thoughts please call the national  suicide prevention lifeline at  1-800-273-talk  that's 1-800-273-8255  [Music]

